# Page object rules

- One class per page/component: `DashboardPage`, `TasksPage`, `TaskForm`, `TaskDetails` (extend `BasePage` for routed pages).
- Expose `readonly` Locators + intention-revealing async actions (`openCreateForm`, `searchFor`, `deleteTask`).
- Locator priority: `getByRole` (with accessible name) → `getByLabel` → `getByTestId` (existing data-testid) → text → CSS (documented).
- Page objects may contain *state-confirming* expectations (e.g. dialog closed after save) but business assertions belong in specs.
- No test data creation, no API calls, no sleeps inside page objects.
- Native `window.confirm()` is handled with `page.once('dialog', ...)` registered BEFORE the click.
- Export new page objects from `pages/index.ts` and add a fixture in `fixtures/test.ts`.
